# Every type declared here is either instantiated somewhere the view's root
# (Main.qml) reaches, or carries an `# UNINSTANTIATED:` line saying why it is
# not. `dialectica-ui/tests/check_qml_reachable.py` enforces that, and it
# computes reachability TRANSITIVELY from Main.qml rather than asking whether a
# name appears somewhere — a type instantiated only by an unreachable type is
# not reachable, and a check that could not tell those apart would have passed
# the whole unmounted island this rule exists to catch.
#
# A record is not an exemption list. It states WHY, because a type held back by
# a scope decision and a type nobody noticed present identically from the
# registration alone, and the reason is the only thing that tells them apart.

singleton DTheme 1.0 DTheme.qml
singleton Core 1.0 Core.qml
singleton DStoaReference 1.0 DStoaReference.qml
Identicon 1.0 Identicon.qml
AddressLabel 1.0 AddressLabel.qml

# UNINSTANTIATED: the name-disjointness gate's measurement apparatus, and it
# MUST stay uninstantiated. `tst_identicon.qml` asserts it exposes no renderer
# at all — no `render`, `name`, `text`, `words` or wordlist — on the ground that
# a renderer would move it under `Malformed key material is refused rather than
# crashed on`, at which point its zero-padding of a short key becomes the defect
# that requirement names: a name attributable to nobody rendered as one
# attributable to somebody. Wiring this breaks the gate.
DKeyNameWindow 1.0 DKeyNameWindow.qml

